WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.015
What does your AI cost, and where does it go?

00:00:04.015 --> 00:00:07.148
This video shows the AI Usage Analytics report:

00:00:07.148 --> 00:00:11.641
every request that is sent to an AI service, grouped by model, feature

00:00:11.641 --> 00:00:16.607
and purpose, the chat completions, the talk time of automated phone calls, and

00:00:16.607 --> 00:00:20.390
how to build your own usage reports in the Report Builder.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:29.998
Which models does your site use, and how many requests does each one get?

00:00:29.998 --> 00:00:34.880
One answer can take several requests, and every one of them is counted.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.485
Which feature made the requests:

00:00:38.485 --> 00:00:43.067
chat, text messages, voice calls, the API or workflows?

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.119
And why:

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:47.650
to answer, to search, to index documents?

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.981
How many tokens, cached tokens, audio minutes, spoken characters and images?

00:00:53.981 --> 00:00:57.860
These are the units that your AI provider bills in.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:00:59.117
And how long do the automated AI phone calls last, and how many

00:00:59.117 --> 00:00:59.330
are handed to a person?

00:01:03.574 --> 00:01:08.360
Usage is recorded only while the AI Usage Analytics feature is on, so

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.359
nothing used before that can be reported.

00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:13.784
Enable it under Tools, Features.

00:01:13.784 --> 00:01:17.804
The report then appears under Reports, Billing and Usage.

00:01:18.256 --> 00:01:22.672
To build your own reports from the same records, also enable the Report

00:01:22.672 --> 00:01:25.597
Builder, which brings Data Pipelines with it.

00:01:25.597 --> 00:01:30.242
The usage records are indexed by AI Chat Session Analytics, so that feature

00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:31.676
must be on as well.

00:01:35.921 --> 00:01:39.887
Open Reports, Billing and Usage, and AI Usage Analytics.

00:01:39.887 --> 00:01:43.918
Choose a Date range, such as the last 30 days, and if you

00:01:43.918 --> 00:01:45.645
like, one AI profile.

00:01:45.645 --> 00:01:47.053
Then click Show.

00:01:47.053 --> 00:01:53.131
The report needs the View AI Chat Analytics permission, the same one as the chat reports.

00:01:53.585 --> 00:01:58.321
Metered usage counts every request that was sent to an AI service, one

00:01:58.321 --> 00:02:01.062
row for each provider, model and kind:

00:02:01.062 --> 00:02:04.676
chat, embeddings, images, speech, or realtime voice.

00:02:04.676 --> 00:02:09.910
One reply can take several requests, such as searching your knowledge and then

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:13.025
writing the answer, and each one is counted.

00:02:13.482 --> 00:02:17.421
Next to the requests are the tokens in and out, and the cached

00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:20.666
input, which providers usually bill at a discount.

00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:25.648
Reasoning, audio, minutes, characters and images are the other units, and a dash

00:02:25.648 --> 00:02:28.776
means that the model is not billed in that unit.

00:02:28.776 --> 00:02:32.542
These are the figures to compare with your provider's bill.

00:02:32.995 --> 00:02:37.876
Audio usage covers only speech to text and text to speech, with the

00:02:37.876 --> 00:02:41.219
hours of audio, the characters and the size.

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:44.295
This site has none, so the page says so.

00:02:44.772 --> 00:02:52.092
Chat completions shows the provider calls, the chat sessions, the chat interactions and the total tokens.

00:02:52.092 --> 00:02:57.631
The table gives the calls, sessions, input, output and tokens, and the average

00:02:57.631 --> 00:03:00.202
latency, for each user and model.

00:03:00.655 --> 00:03:04.102
The Voice section covers automated AI phone calls.

00:03:04.102 --> 00:03:07.735
It stays empty here, because this site has made none.

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:17.786
Group metered usage by Model and category to see which feature made the requests.

00:03:17.786 --> 00:03:24.218
Chat sessions, chat interactions, text messages, voice calls, the API, workflows and other

00:03:24.218 --> 00:03:26.697
agents each get their own rows.

00:03:27.161 --> 00:03:30.947
Model and purpose shows why the requests were made:

00:03:30.947 --> 00:03:36.660
to answer, to search, to index documents, to transcribe, to summarize, and more.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.781
Services that you add can name their own.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.711
Group completions by AI profile to see which assistant used the tokens, and

00:03:44.711 --> 00:03:46.697
how many chat sessions it had.

00:03:46.697 --> 00:03:50.505
That is the table to read when you want to know which assistant

00:03:50.505 --> 00:03:52.050
is the most expensive.

00:03:52.721 --> 00:03:57.403
Or group them by connection, to see which AI service account was used.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:01.716
A connection holds the address and the key of an AI service, and

00:04:01.716 --> 00:04:03.995
several profiles can share one.

00:04:03.995 --> 00:04:08.061
The other choices are user and model, model, and deployment.

00:04:09.852 --> 00:04:16.142
Voice calls can be grouped by deployment, AI profile, campaign, channel, engine or

00:04:16.142 --> 00:04:20.072
day, and audio usage by model, voice or language.

00:04:24.272 --> 00:04:28.344
Calls is the number of automated calls, and AI minutes is how long

00:04:28.344 --> 00:04:30.492
the callers heard the assistant.

00:04:31.242 --> 00:04:35.769
Caller minutes is how long the caller spoke, and silence minutes is how

00:04:35.769 --> 00:04:39.472
long nobody did, on the calls where this can be measured.

00:04:40.222 --> 00:04:44.281
Average call is the average length of the assistant's part of a call,

00:04:44.281 --> 00:04:48.502
and handoff rate is the share of calls that were handed to a live agent.

00:04:49.252 --> 00:04:53.743
Barge-ins per call shows how often callers talked over the assistant.

00:04:53.743 --> 00:04:58.712
A figure that a kind of call cannot measure is left out, not counted as zero.

00:05:02.865 --> 00:05:06.834
The usage records are also data sets of the AI chat data source,

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:10.973
so the Report Builder can build your own reports from them, such as

00:05:10.973 --> 00:05:12.731
the tokens of each model.

00:05:12.731 --> 00:05:15.565
Create a new report, and click Add data set.

00:05:16.016 --> 00:05:20.515
Under AI chat you find AI completion usage, with one row for each

00:05:20.515 --> 00:05:24.951
request that was sent to an AI service, and AI voice usage, with

00:05:24.951 --> 00:05:27.106
one row for each phone call.

00:05:27.106 --> 00:05:30.845
Chat sessions and Chat session metrics are there too.

00:05:30.845 --> 00:05:32.746
Add AI completion usage.

00:05:33.197 --> 00:05:37.710
Drag Model and Total token count to the columns, and the preview shows

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.551
the tokens of each model.

00:05:39.551 --> 00:05:44.717
A calculated field with your provider's prices turns them into an estimated cost.

00:05:48.917 --> 00:05:52.314
Compare the metered usage with your provider's invoice.

00:05:52.314 --> 00:05:57.437
The tables count requests, so they match what is billed, not only what the chats show.

00:05:58.187 --> 00:06:01.689
Watch the cached input and the model of each feature.

00:06:01.689 --> 00:06:07.447
A cheaper model for searching or summarizing can cut the bill without touching the answers.

00:06:08.197 --> 00:06:12.186
Usage is recorded only from the moment the feature is on, so turn

00:06:12.186 --> 00:06:14.097
it on early, and keep it on.

00:06:16.097 --> 00:06:21.256
Turn on the usage analytics, let your assistants work, and read where the tokens go.

00:06:21.256 --> 00:06:22.747
Thanks for watching.

